{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 42, :comments ["<b>And it was told to Rebekah.</b> By the holy spirit it was told to her what Esau was plotting in his heart." "<b>Comforts himself concerning you.</b> He was consoled over the brotherhood, to think another thought — to disown you and kill you. And its midrash: you are already dead in his eyes and he has drunk the cup of consolations over you. According to its plain sense, it is a term of consolation — he comforts himself over the blessings by killing you."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:00:50.689529166Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}